{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics","id":1230227,"title":"Question on Kuei-Jin metaphysics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-26T03:41:33-07:00","id":1230227,"title":"Question on Kuei-Jin metaphysics","content":"Here's a short question from me who don't know anything about the Kindred of the East, and I'd prefer not to have to go through that big book just to get this question answered.<br /> <br /> That is that in the 19th (and early 20th as I understand it) century lots of Chinese immigrated to the US and set up shop, among other things resulting in the creation of the Tongs which will be of some importance in my possible gangster focused chronicle in the 1920s and 1930s.<br /> <br /> BUT<br /> <br /> I have a question regarding these Chinese immigrants and Kuei-Jin. Is there any reasonable risk, or chance, that Kuei-Jin would arise among their dead or come with them this early in history? I understand that Kuei-Jin arises in &quot;Asia&quot; from India and on east and I know they made this move out from Asia into Anglophone aeas in the metaplot around the year 2000. But in the 1920-1930s period would there be any presence?<br /> <br /> I mostly plan on making the Chinese vampires as Cainites from the standard clans but I thought that I should check to got my base covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T04:05:25-07:00","id":1230231,"title":"","content":"Canon-wise I believe not.<br /> <br /> personally, I think it would be quite fitting, maybe have them be part of Heretic group instead of the Big 5, and voil\u00e0! California had such a big Asian communities with strong traditions, it make sense that they would Arise there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T04:08:51-07:00","id":1230232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230231#post1230231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canon-wise I believe not.<br /> <br /> personally, I think it would be quite fitting, maybe have them be part of Heretic group instead of the Big 5, and voil\u00e0! California had such a big Asian communities with strong traditions, it make sense that they would Arise there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for a quick reply!<br /> <br /> This is kind of the info I was looking for. I think I'll probably pass on the Kuei-Jin then and just make the Chinese vampires as Kindred from the standard Clans as I don't need to learn a whole new rule system for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T08:30:52-07:00","id":1230291,"title":"","content":"Quick answer: kuei-jin are sort of ghosts that escape their local Hell and return to their own bodies and incidentally sustain themselves with the blood of the living, but they aren't related with Cainites. Therefore they don't have clans, but sort of distinction lines based on their beliefs (akin to Cainite's path of enlightment).<br /> Straight jumping all the metaphisic, a Kuei-jin <b>could</b> spontaneously rise from the asian communities, but he would be a sort of &quot;caitiff&quot;, without no one to educate him on the way of his strain. Actually, most probably he would just stay around as some sort of <i>wight</i> (vampire whose Humanity/Enlightenment is down to 0 and is, effectively, a predatory beast).<br /> <br /> There could be some stray Kuei-jin going around in the era you mentioned, but they are just people going around to see the world. Definitely not the norm nor a common case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T14:38:02-07:00","id":1230368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics#post1230227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a short question from me who don't know anything about the Kindred of the East, and I'd prefer not to have to go through that big book just to get this question answered.<br /> <br /> That is that in the 19th (and early 20th as I understand it) century lots of Chinese immigrated to the US and set up shop, among other things resulting in the creation of the Tongs which will be of some importance in my possible gangster focused chronicle in the 1920s and 1930s.<br /> <br /> BUT<br /> <br /> I have a question regarding these Chinese immigrants and Kuei-Jin. Is there any reasonable risk, or chance, that Kuei-Jin would arise among their dead or come with them this early in history? I understand that Kuei-Jin arises in &quot;Asia&quot; from India and on east and I know they made this move out from Asia into Anglophone aeas in the metaplot around the year 2000. But in the 1920-1930s period would there be any presence?<br /> <br /> I mostly plan on making the Chinese vampires as Cainites from the standard clans but I thought that I should check to got my base covered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> According to the book that cover Victorian times, yes. They were rising that early in those areas, there were full minicourts in chinatowns by the turn of the 20th century. Even pre KJ as they would be portrayed eventually when they were previously something more embracey but still a separate thing from Kindred in the earliest novels they were holding china towns.<br /> <br /> That said Its your game. You shouldn't feel any need to be beholden to some measure of &quot;canon&quot;(and even that's a moving target depending on the book) KOTE is a complicated book which requires HEAVY House Ruling, and I wouldn't suggest you need to run some sort of &quot;sim&quot; woD vs what works for you. Either making them Standard or Kindred with various rule breaks would be the easiest ways to do it. I mean if they are NPCs if they can do something like &quot;not take damage from the sun&quot; or shrug off True Faith, it just makes them more mysterious.<br /> <br /> If they are meant to be players I'd honestly drop them unless you really want to engage with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T15:13:33-07:00","id":1230378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230291#post1230291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick answer: kuei-jin are sort of ghosts that escape their local Hell and return to their own bodies and incidentally sustain themselves with the blood of the living, but they aren't related with Cainites. Therefore they don't have clans, but sort of distinction lines based on their beliefs (akin to Cainite's path of enlightment).<br /> Straight jumping all the metaphisic, a Kuei-jin <b>could</b> spontaneously rise from the asian communities, but he would be a sort of &quot;caitiff&quot;, without no one to educate him on the way of his strain. Actually, most probably he would just stay around as some sort of <i>wight</i> (vampire whose Humanity/Enlightenment is down to 0 and is, effectively, a predatory beast).<br /> <br /> There could be some stray Kuei-jin going around in the era you mentioned, but they are just people going around to see the world. Definitely not the norm nor a common case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there are the Kanbujian, Kuei-jin that rise outside of their sphere of influence and manage to overcome their initial P'o-driven frenzy.<br /> <br /> So yeah Gurkhal, you can have Kuei-jin outside of Eastern Asia and their Courts just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T23:32:17-07:00","id":1230472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230291#post1230291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick answer: kuei-jin are sort of ghosts that escape their local Hell and return to their own bodies and incidentally sustain themselves with the blood of the living, but they aren't related with Cainites. Therefore they don't have clans, but sort of distinction lines based on their beliefs (akin to Cainite's path of enlightment).<br /> Straight jumping all the metaphisic, a Kuei-jin <b>could</b> spontaneously rise from the asian communities, but he would be a sort of &quot;caitiff&quot;, without no one to educate him on the way of his strain. Actually, most probably he would just stay around as some sort of <i>wight</i> (vampire whose Humanity/Enlightenment is down to 0 and is, effectively, a predatory beast).<br /> <br /> There could be some stray Kuei-jin going around in the era you mentioned, but they are just people going around to see the world. Definitely not the norm nor a common case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I get you. Having animalistic monsters is something that I don't need the added the Kuei-Jin rule system for and lone explorers may probably not wind up in the gangster business just like that. Although it could be interesting to throw in a Devil Tiger or something to shake things up a little and give the players something to compete with that don't play by the rules they are used to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230368#post1230368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the book that cover Victorian times, yes. They were rising that early in those areas, there were full minicourts in chinatowns by the turn of the 20th century. Even pre KJ as they would be portrayed eventually when they were previously something more embracey but still a separate thing from Kindred in the earliest novels they were holding china towns.<br /> <br /> That said Its your game. You shouldn't feel any need to be beholden to some measure of &quot;canon&quot;(and even that's a moving target depending on the book) KOTE is a complicated book which requires HEAVY House Ruling, and I wouldn't suggest you need to run some sort of &quot;sim&quot; woD vs what works for you. Either making them Standard or Kindred with various rule breaks would be the easiest ways to do it. I mean if they are NPCs if they can do something like &quot;not take damage from the sun&quot; or shrug off True Faith, it just makes them more mysterious.<br /> <br /> If they are meant to be players I'd honestly drop them unless you really want to engage with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean &quot;Sunset Empires&quot;? I think I've got that and will take a closer look in it for more information.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Kindred of the East does sounds like a lot of extra rules, reading and balancing for what would essentially be a fairly minor part of the game. So I think I'll skip the Kuei-Jin and run the Chinese vampires as Kindred. Namely that some Kindred Embraced Chinese immigrants, who in turn Embraced more people and after a while you had a bunch of people running around in the night who were ethnically Chinese, or Chinese Americans, but metaphysically Cainites. I feel this may be an easier way to go about it.<br /> <br /> I hope that makes some kind of sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230378#post1230378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, there are the Kanbujian, Kuei-jin that rise outside of their sphere of influence and manage to overcome their initial P'o-driven frenzy.<br /> <br /> So yeah Gurkhal, you can have Kuei-jin outside of Eastern Asia and their Courts just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting but given the above mentioned rule wise work I think I'll pass for now. But this opening to introduce Kuei-Jin at a later stage is a window I don't want to close but rather see what use I can potentially have for it in the future depending on where the game goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T02:44:37-07:00","id":1230484,"title":"","content":"Remember the big thing, Nothing stops you from using Kindred Rules and KOTE Fluff. Like the PCs find they can't diab this person for some reason. OR that staking Fails OR they can do some wierd stuff that they can't learn. Even if you are generally using Blood points and Standard discplines for most of their powers. I mean the Players aren't going to see under the hood after all, if you want to run a Devil Tiger who's running Quietus, Potence and chimestry they don't get to see it they just get to see whatever outcomes you fluff it as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T03:23:10-07:00","id":1230487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230484#post1230484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the big thing, Nothing stops you from using Kindred Rules and KOTE Fluff. Like the PCs find they can't diab this person for some reason. OR that staking Fails OR they can do some wierd stuff that they can't learn. Even if you are generally using Blood points and Standard discplines for most of their powers. I mean the Players aren't going to see under the hood after all, if you want to run a Devil Tiger who's running Quietus, Potence and chimestry they don't get to see it they just get to see whatever outcomes you fluff it as.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that, but I think I'll try out my solution and see where takes my group. I can always introduce Kuei-Jin at a later stage if it would add to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T04:37:40-07:00","id":1230493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230472#post1230472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I get you. Having animalistic monsters is something that I don't need the added the Kuei-Jin rule system for and lone explorers may probably not wind up in the gangster business just like that. Although it could be interesting to throw in a Devil Tiger or something to shake things up a little and give the players something to compete with that don't play by the rules they are used to.</div> </div> </div> </div>yup, I too did that a couple times in the past<br /> <br /> also you can use the Kanbujian thing mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar420_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"420\" data-vbnamecard=\"420\">AkatsukiLeader13</a> , how your players will act with a vampire that doesn't know what he is but just doesn't play on the Kindred's rules? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T05:00:39-07:00","id":1230498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230493#post1230493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yup, I too did that a couple times in the past<br /> <br /> also you can use the Kanbujian thing mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar420_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"420\" data-vbnamecard=\"420\">AkatsukiLeader13</a> , how your players will act with a vampire that doesn't know what he is but just doesn't play on the Kindred's rules? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've considered it but will pass for now.<br /> <br /> If the games goes on for further than the traditional 1920-1933 prohibition era, I may throw in the Kuei-Jin as the gangster scene is likely to calm down a bit when bootlegging isn't around as a lucrative business. In that case it might be that these Kanbujian guys shows up with a few that overcomes their primal state and eventually some Kuei-Jin explorer or globetrotter comes around and teach them a thing or two to set them onthe path, with a potential conflict between them and the Cainites.<br /> <br /> But right now I'm trying to avoid my habit of bloating my plans and focus on gangster era action with Cainites in the centre.<br /> <br /> But please note that while my responses may be short, I do read and consider everything posted here. And there are lots of good stuff that I didn't know about, angles and ideas that I hadn't thought about. I know that some posts have been fairly short. I'm not a man of long phrases and many words at most times, but I really appreciate all the feedback and suggestions I'm getting here. Even ones that I will not use for this game are ones that I can use for future games.<br /> <br /> So please, keep them coming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":".  Had a mentioning that probably served little actual purpose. So I removed it. 06-27-2018, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T13:15:34-07:00","id":1230625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230487#post1230487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True that, but I think I'll try out my solution and see where takes my group. I can always introduce Kuei-Jin at a later stage if it would add to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean when/if you do I'm suggesting you just modify the Kindred template rather than try to run fully from the book. IT requires Significant House ruling and understanding to make work. IF you just have some npcs running around making them &quot;kindred with weird powers and weird beliefs' isn't going to change much for the players fighting them, I mean honestly the difference between a KJ and Sabbat or Independent on a Path isn't going to be all that much to your Cam or anarch Neonate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T13:54:38-07:00","id":1230635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230625#post1230625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean when/if you do I'm suggesting you just modify the Kindred template rather than try to run fully from the book. IT requires Significant House ruling and understanding to make work. IF you just have some npcs running around making them &quot;kindred with weird powers and weird beliefs' isn't going to change much for the players fighting them, I mean honestly the difference between a KJ and Sabbat or Independent on a Path isn't going to be all that much to your Cam or anarch Neonate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you and you make alot of sense. I skipped through some of the book and it looked like very taxing reading and lots of rules. And I play WoD mostly due to the relative lack of rules and focus on storytelling. Modifying the Kindred and maybe throw in some not-before-seen disciplines seems like a much easier solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T14:09:27-07:00","id":1230637,"title":"","content":"My ruling is to draw on MtA and what matters is local consensus. If the dominant local belief is in reincarnation and the possibility of a temporary he\u2019ll between lives, then the Yama Kings can claim souls from that area and souls can escape and Kuei Jin can rise.<br /> <br /> So if you have a thriving \u201cChina town\u201d in the West, you can have a strong enough localized consensus for KJ to rise.<br /> <br /> An individual\u2019s personal beliefs or blood ancestry are less relevant than local ambient consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T05:43:38-07:00","id":1252493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230637#post1230637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ruling is to draw on MtA and what matters is local consensus. If the dominant local belief is in reincarnation and the possibility of a temporary he\u2019ll between lives, then the Yama Kings can claim souls from that area and souls can escape and Kuei Jin can rise.<br /> <br /> So if you have a thriving \u201cChina town\u201d in the West, you can have a strong enough localized consensus for KJ to rise.<br /> <br /> An individual\u2019s personal beliefs or blood ancestry are less relevant than local ambient consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. If you don't become a Wraith, your soul goes where you truly expect it to, with some fairness applied since these heavens and hells have standards; you don't go to hell for irrationally hating yourself, a big ego and denial don't get you into heaven.<br /> <br /> Some Asians have strong enough belief in the Hungry Dead that they return as one, some people get chosen by Osiris (or other entities) to return as mummies, some people become Wraiths but immediately try and become Risen...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T11:04:26-07:00","id":1253107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1230227-question-on-kuei-jin-metaphysics?p=1230637#post1230637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> <br /> An individual\u2019s personal beliefs or blood ancestry are less relevant than local ambient consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that this part is most fitting of this in regards to how it should be in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-10-2018, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}